{"id":"4db3fb1b352613f1d2d0209eae58c435c00c2dadfe1832e89bf33e4d21566a7f","pubkey":"6fef3f60b36498c4da71345661f08566bec95a3ee195bd3fd853b49bf2f29200","created_at":1782776407,"content":"https://blossom.smartflow.social/85be326ab1ad1379b5cd977a6ce8e9984894005901109c789b975eaf9818157a.jpg\nRaw Honey\n\nFood made by insects, not factories.\n\nBees collect nectar.\nThey dry it, seal it, and leave it in wax.\n\nHumans valued it because it kept.\nSweetness used to come with work, weather, and stings.\n\nNow sweetness arrives as syrup in a tanker.\nNo hive.\nNo season.\nJust a pump.","tags":[]}
